WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.734
The lasting message is a change of workflow.

00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:07.787
Instead of designing a graph network and then
hoping to prove it is expressive,

00:00:07.867 --> 00:00:12.264
you can start from a language whose expressive
power you already know,

00:00:12.344 --> 00:00:16.996
reduce it to a clean grammar, and read the network
straight off the rules,

00:00:17.076 --> 00:00:19.682
expressiveness guaranteed by construction.

00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:25.311
G2N2 is the concrete payoff of that idea: a
provably 3-W-L model that is faster and more

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.293
accurate than its predecessors.

00:00:27.373 --> 00:00:29.660
And because the framework is generic,

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:35.032
the same grammatical route could turn other
algebraic fragments into other networks,

00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:37.910
each carrying its expressive power by design.
